From: Codex <codex@openai.local>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 02:56:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] The 700-token completion cap was throwing away half of every
 seat call

MEASURED BY EXPERIMENT, NOT BY READING. Twelve real rows off the deepening queue, same prompts,
same model, same temperature; only the completion cap varied, crossed with
`response_format: json_object` so that "the model will not emit JSON" and "the model was cut off
before it finished emitting JSON" could be told apart:

    max_tokens=700,  no response_format     6/12 parsed    50%
    max_tokens=700,  response_format json   7/12 parsed    58%
    max_tokens=3000, no response_format    12/12 parsed   100%
    max_tokens=3000, response_format json  12/12 parsed   100%

THE CAUSE IS TRUNCATION, NOT COMPLIANCE. Structured output barely moves the number (+8pp) while
the cap moves it to perfect, and it is perfect with structured output switched OFF -- so the
model was always willing to answer and was being cut off mid-object. `extract()` asks for
`reasoning_effort: high`, OpenAI-compatible endpoints charge reasoning tokens against the
completion cap, and a reasoning model spends 700 tokens thinking before it writes anything.
`_parse` then finds no closing brace and the caller records "reply was not a JSON object", which
reads like a model that refused.

WHAT IT COST, measured live the day before on the trading box: 456 of 789 completed calls -- 58%
-- died exactly that way. That is the single largest loss in the desk's only novel-mechanism
lane, and the arm-A failure rate above (50%) reproduces it.

IT COSTS NOTHING TO FIX. The free tier is capped in REQUESTS PER DAY, not tokens -- the provider's
own counter says so (`llm_seat.provider_free_quota`: free_model_daily_requests {used, limit,
remaining}) -- so the same thousand requests simply come back usable. At the measured 13.1%
recovery rate per PARSED reply, recovering those 456 is worth roughly +60 recovered mechanisms a
day against 30 today: about three times the desk's novel-mechanism discovery rate, for no money,
no permission and no gate touched. The recovered rows face the identical ten gates; this adds
arrivals, never leniency, and fixed_trial_count is unchanged.

The number is an env-overridable constant rather than a literal, so the next person to measure it
can move it without hunting through a call site.

